From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: V <61495413+kelo221@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 18 Oct 2026 03:22:58 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] Soloud::mix_internal: a mix of no frames keeps the last
 visualization data

With ENABLE_VISUALIZATION, a mix of no frames (Soloud::mix with 0
samples) took the short-mix path, which reads the mix at `i % aSamples`:
an integer division by zero that crashes on x86. A mix of no frames now
leaves the wave data and channel volumes as the last mix set them.
---
 src/core/soloud.cpp | 4 +++-
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/core/soloud.cpp b/src/core/soloud.cpp
index 26246a6..ef4cd4e 100644
--- a/src/core/soloud.cpp
+++ b/src/core/soloud.cpp
@@ -2311,7 +2311,9 @@ namespace SoLoud
 		// The buffers should be large enough for it, we just may do a few bytes of unneccessary work.
 		clip_internal(mOutputScratch, mScratch, aStride, globalVolume[0], globalVolume[1]);
 
-		if (mFlags & ENABLE_VISUALIZATION)
+		// A mix of no frames has nothing to show: keep the last data (the
+		// short-mix path below would divide by zero).
+		if ((mFlags & ENABLE_VISUALIZATION) && aSamples > 0)
 		{
 			for (i = 0; i < MAX_CHANNELS; i++)
 			{
